## What I did

**`src/cli.rs`** — split the dotenv loader:
• Added `pub fn load_dotenv_from(dir: &Path) — reads dir/.env`, parses via parse_dotenv, returns empty map on missing/unreadable file (same best-effort contract).
• `load_cwd_dotenv()` is now a one-liner delegating to `load_dotenv_from(Path::new("."))`. Behavior for product users is byte-for-byte unchanged; `resolve_api_key_env` untouched.
• Added 3 hermetic tests (all in the existing `cli.rs` test module, no `set_current_dir`, no new file):
  • `test_load_dotenv_from_reads_file` — real `.env` in a temp dir, asserts key/value + comment skipped, cleans up.
  • `test_load_dotenv_from_missing_file_returns_empty` — nonexistent dir → empty map, no panic.
  • `test_load_dotenv_from_export_and_quotes_via_file` — one integration-ish case: export  prefix, quoted value, inline # via real file.

**`docs/src/contributing/testing.md`** — added the one-sentence convention: `.env`-loading tests should use `load_dotenv_from(temp_dir), never set_current_dir`.

Verification: `cargo fmt -- --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo build, cargo test` (88 passed) all green. The 3 new tests were confirmed to actually run and pass.

No scope expansion: precedence, search order, and `resolve_api_key_env` semantics unchanged; no home-dir support added. CLAUDE.md's cli.rs bullet doesn't name `load_cwd_dotenv`, so no edit was needed there.
